body:
`@object-ui/types` `DashboardWidgetSchema` required `id` and `component` fields, but `@objectstack/spec` v3.0.4 defines widgets using `type`/`options` shorthand. This type mismatch forced unsafe `as any` casts throughout the renderer and left metric widgets without proper React keys (`key={undefined}` for all 4 cards), causing reconciliation issues.

### Types (`packages/types`)

- Made `id` and `component` optional on `DashboardWidgetSchema`
- Added `type?: string` and `options?: unknown` to match the spec shorthand format
- Updated both the TypeScript interface and Zod schema

```typescript
// Before: only legacy format
interface DashboardWidgetSchema {
  id: string;
  component: SchemaNode;
  // ...
}

// After: supports both legacy and spec shorthand
interface DashboardWidgetSchema {
  id?: string;
  component?: SchemaNode;
  type?: string;
  options?: unknown;
  // ...
}
```

### Renderer (`packages/plugin-dashboard`)

- Removed all `(widget as any).type` / `(widget as any).options` casts — types now cover both formats
- Fixed key generation: `widget.id || widget.title || \`widget-${index}\`` prevents duplicate `undefined` keys on metric widgets
- Same fixes applied to `DashboardGridLayout.tsx`

### Tests

- Added test for spec shorthand metric widget rendering (type + options at widget level)
- Added test verifying unique keys across multiple widgets without `id`/`title`

